  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 21,
    "summary": "Job admits that the wicked sometimes prosper in this life—Then he testifies that their judgment will be hereafter in the day of wrath and destruction.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "But Job answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear diligently my speech, and let this be your consolations.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Suffer me that I may speak; and after that I have spoken, mock on.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Job 16:20 (10, 20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "As for me, is my complaint to man? and if it were so, why should not my spirit be troubled?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Mark me, and be astonished, and lay your hand upon your mouth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Judg. 18:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Judg. 18:19.",
            "prettyString": "Judges 18:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "judges",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 18,
                    "end": 18,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Even when I remember I am afraid, and trembling taketh hold on my flesh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore do the wicked live, become old, yea, are mighty in power?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Job 12:6; Hel. 7:5 (5–6). TG Worldliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Their seed is established in their sight with them, and their offspring before their eyes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Their houses are safe from fear, neither is the rod of God upon them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Their bull gendereth, and faileth not; their cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "They send forth their little ones like a flock, and their children dance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "They take the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "HEB flute."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "They spend their days in wealth, and in a moment go down to the grave.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore they say unto God, Depart from us; for we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "What is the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what profit should we have, if we pray unto him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Lo, their good is not in their hand: the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "How oft is the candle of the wicked put out! and how oft cometh their destruction upon them! God distributeth sorrows in his anger.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 56
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "They are as stubble before the wind, and as chaff that the storm carrieth away.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Ps. 1:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 1:4.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 1:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "God layeth up his iniquity for his children: he rewardeth him, and he shall know it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Reward."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Reward.",
            "prettyString": "TG Reward",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Reward",
                "entryId": "tg-reward",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "His eyes shall see his destruction, and he shall drink of the wrath of the Almighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Ps. 75:8; Mosiah 3:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 75:8; Mosiah 3:18.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 75:8; Mosiah 3:18",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 75,
                    "end": 75,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 3,
                    "end": 3,
