            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I know your thoughts, and the devices which ye wrongfully imagine against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye say, Where is the house of the prince? and where are the dwelling places of the wicked?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Have ye not asked them that go by the way? and do ye not know their tokens,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "That the wicked is reserved to the day of destruction? they shall be brought forth to the day of wrath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Who shall declare his way to his face? and who shall repay him what he hath done?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Retribution."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Retribution.",
            "prettyString": "TG Retribution",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Retribution",
                "entryId": "tg-retribution",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet shall he be brought to the grave, and shall remain in the tomb.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "The clods of the valley shall be sweet unto him, and every man shall draw after him, as there are innumerable before him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 21:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
